cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite this repository."
title: "Lean formalization of the I3322 variational identity and nonattainment for finite-dimensional pure-projective strategies"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Pauwels"
    given-names: "Jef"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jefpauwels/i3322-lean"
url: "https://github.com/jefpauwels/i3322-lean"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization proving that the supremum of the explicitly defined
  I3322 Bell functional over finite-dimensional complex bipartite pure-state
  strategies with three binary projective measurements per party equals the
  supremum over finite Pál–Vértesi chains, and that no strategy in this
  pure-projective class attains that supremum. The standard reduction from
  mixed states and binary POVMs to this class is not formalized.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - quantum information
  - quantum nonlocality
  - Bell inequalities
  - I3322
